# Dev Tools
#
# List of dev tools I prefer. The list is ordered: highest preference comes
# first, within each Category. The configuration in this repo mostly revolves
# around these tools, and a few more. This file is under development, so more
# tools will be added.
#
# Only current tools and AI tools go here. Tools I tried, used before, or want
# to try go in work dev_tools_archive.md:
# https://github.com/raveensrk/work/blob/main/deck/tools/dev_tools_archive.md
# A tool lives in one file only.
#
# Level is how hard a tool is to learn well, not how much I prefer it:
#   1 Beginner      useful within minutes
#   2 Easy          the basics take a few hours
#   3 Intermediate  takes days; has its own concepts or config to learn
#   4 Advanced      takes weeks; needs a deep mental model
#   5 Expert        takes months or years to master
#
# Tier is how much a tool matters to me, not how hard it is: base is the
# core kit, extra adds what I use often, max is everything. Views build on
# each other (extra shows base too), so a tool never requires one of a higher
# tier.
#
# Requires is my own learning path: the tool must be known before this one.
# Each Requires line must be met (AND); `A | B` on one line means either one
# (OR). A prerequisite never has a higher Level than the tool it unlocks, and
# a prerequisite already implied through another one is not repeated.
#
# Validate:  recfix --check dev_tools.rec
# Query:     recsel -e 'Level = 1' -p Name dev_tools.rec
# Charts:    ./dev_tools.py   (writes dev_tools.svg, the level map,
#                              dev_tools_path.svg, the prerequisites, and
#                              dev_tools.html, the prerequisites by tier)

%rec: Tool
%key: Name
%type: Level range 1 5
%type: Tier enum base extra max
%mandatory: Name Category Level Tier
%allowed: Name Category Subcategory Level Tier Requires Url Note

